   "stem": {
      "text": "The graph of the polar curve \\( r = 5 \\sin{\\left(\\theta \\right)} + 8 \\) for \\( 0.3 \\le \\theta \\le 1.9 \\) is shown. Using a calculator, find the value of \\( \\theta \\) that corresponds to the point on the curve farthest from the y-axis. Justify your answer, show the setup, and give the value correct to three decimal places.",
      "setup_required": true,
      "command_verb": "find"
   },
   "answer_key": {
      "form": "numeric",
      "mathjson": 0.4250911711334801,
      "decimals": 3
   },
   "worked_solution": [
      {
         "step": 1,
         "text": "The distance from the y-axis is \\( |x| \\), where \\( x = r\\cos\\theta = \\left(5 \\sin{\\left(\\theta \\right)} + 8\\right) \\cos{\\left(\\theta \\right)} \\).",
         "point_type_id": "BC-PT-99005",
         "rule_named": "polar to rectangular conversion"
      },
      {
         "step": 2,
         "text": "Set \\( \\frac{dx}{d\\theta} = - \\left(5 \\sin{\\left(\\theta \\right)} + 8\\right) \\sin{\\left(\\theta \\right)} + 5 \\cos^{2}{\\left(\\theta \\right)} = 0 \\). On the interval a calculator gives one solution, \\( \\theta \\approx 0.425 \\).",
         "mathjson": 0.4250911711334801,
         "point_type_id": "BC-PT-99013",
         "rule_named": "critical angle"
      },
      {
         "step": 3,
         "text": "Compare the candidates, the critical angle and both endpoints: \\( |x(0.3)| \\approx 9.054 \\), \\( |x(0.425)| \\approx 9.167 \\), \\( |x(1.9)| \\approx 4.116 \\). The largest distance is at \\( \\theta \\approx 0.425 \\), so that is the farthest point.",
         "point_type_id": "BC-PT-99011",
         "rule_named": "candidates test"
      }
   ],
